# Live Chapter 1 content, ported from existing scenes; Codex integration 2026-09-09.
NPC: gardener
LOCATION: estate

TOPIC: default
  GATE: estate_complete AND coat = plain AND NOT topic_done(gardener, gardener_plain)
  TAG: gardener_plain
  TIME: 3
  VOICE: trombone_cautious_short_v1
  THE GARDENER: "You took the badge off."
  WALTER CORWIN: "I'm still asking."
  VOICE: trombone_cautious_long_v2
  THE GARDENER: "Then write this down as well. I saw the woman here before. Walking to the service door.\n\nI don't know her name. The steward might.\nAsk him as though an answer is required."
  NOTEBOOK: service_door | "The gardener saw the woman at the service door. Ask the steward."

TOPIC: default
  GATE: estate_complete AND visit_count(gardener) >= 2 AND coat = plain
  TAG: gardener_repeat_plain_thorns
  WEIGHT: 3
  VOICE: trombone_dismissive_short_v1
  THE GARDENER: "The rose beds are cut back for winter, Walter. Without the star pinned on, you look like any other man walking through dead canes."

TOPIC: default
  GATE: estate_complete AND visit_count(gardener) >= 2 AND coat = plain
  TAG: gardener_repeat_plain_soil
  WEIGHT: 2
  [He turns a spade of cold earth, his boots coated in dark, sticky leaf-mold.]
  VOICE: trombone_weary_medium_v1
  THE GARDENER: "Ask the steward in the house if you're hunting shadows. I keep the soil, not the silver."

TOPIC: default
  GATE: estate_complete AND visit_count(gardener) >= 2 AND coat != plain
  TAG: gardener_repeat_badge_gravel
  WEIGHT: 3
  VOICE: trombone_neutral_short_v1
  THE GARDENER: "Mind the gravel path, Officer. A precinct boot leaves deep marks where the ground is fresh."

TOPIC: default
  GATE: estate_complete AND visit_count(gardener) >= 2 AND coat != plain
  TAG: gardener_repeat_badge_patrol
  WEIGHT: 2
  VOICE: trombone_dismissive_short_v2
  THE GARDENER: "Odell took the wagon down an hour ago. Standing by the hedge in uniform won't bring the dead back."

TOPIC: default
  GATE: always
  TAG: gardener
  TIME: 3
  VOICE: trombone_dismissive_long_v1
  THE GARDENER: "I keep the roses. I don't keep the hours of the men who walk among them."
  WALTER CORWIN: "You found both scenes?"
  VOICE: trombone_weary_long_v1
  THE GARDENER: "Yes.\n\nI sent for eight sheets.\nThey brought six the first time."
  NOTEBOOK: eight_sheets | "The gardener requested eight sheets. Six arrived first."

